---
// Three failed approaches, set side by side as objects so the reader compares
// them rather than reading a list.
const tried = [
  {
    title: "The internal champion.",
    body: "A senior PM or engineer gets tapped as the AI person. But they have a day job. The old way is easier and less risky. AI stays a side project. This is my only job.",
  },
  {
    title: "The one-off training.",
    body: "Everyone learns generic prompting tricks. Nobody goes back to work and knows what to do next. It doesn't stick because it's not connected to your actual processes. I work on your real data, your real sprint work, your real pipeline.",
  },
  {
    title: "The status quo.",
    body: "You feel the pressure. You bought the licenses. You keep talking about it. Nothing changes.",
  },
];
---

<section class="py-16 md:py-20">
  <div class="container-wide">
    <h2 class="rule-heading mb-10">What you've already tried</h2>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
      {tried.map(({ title, body }) => (
        <div class="panel flex flex-col gap-4 p-6 md:p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl leading-tight">{title}</h3>
          <p class="text-text-body leading-relaxed">{body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="font-display text-3xl md:text-[2.5rem] leading-tight text-text max-w-4xl mt-12 md:mt-14">
      All three fail for the same reason. There's no one showing your team what
      good looks like in the context of your actual business.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
